  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${K}^{\u2032}$, the image of $K(\\sqrt{2},-2)$ under the action of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of $K$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $K:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${K}^{\u2032}.$ Therefore, ${K}^{\u2032}(-4,-8).$",
